      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults, with single doses up to 800 mg. Over-the-counter labeling caps at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose and twice the maximum single dose. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed**, for pain.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd also suggest a pharmacy review for a dose that far above the labeled maximum."
      }
     ],
